        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/1_NSDDo7c.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>Last night, <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/game-awards-2026-nominees-full-list-gta-6\">The Game Awards 2026 nominations were officially announced</a>, and fans immediately noticed the prestigious Game of the Year category - previously won by the likes of <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/astro-bot\">Astro Bot</a>, Clair Obscur, and <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/elden-ring-walkthrough-8042\">Elden Ring</a> - does not feature a PlayStation-published game this year. It's a rare sight for PlayStation Studios, which has secured a Game of the Year nomination every year since 2015.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/playstation-sony-game-awards-no-nominations\">Read more</a></p>",
